# Open Pulse Crawler — environment template
#
# Copy to `.env` at the repo root, then either:
#   • API only:        `docker compose -f infra/docker-compose.yml --env-file ../.env up -d`
#                      → FastAPI on http://localhost:${OPC_API_PORT:-8000}
#   • API + GUI + Nginx: `docker compose -f infra/docker-compose.yml --env-file ../.env --profile gui up -d`
#                      → Browser GUI on http://localhost:${OPC_PORT:-80}
#   • or run the API/CLI directly via `uv run` after exporting the same vars.
#
# All variables marked REQUIRED must be set; everything else has sensible
# defaults baked into either the compose file or the application code.

# ----- REQUIRED: API authentication ----------------------------------------
#
# Bearer token clients must send to authenticated endpoints.
# Generate one with:
#   python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))'
API_TOKEN=

# ----- REQUIRED: GitHub access ---------------------------------------------
#
# GitHub Personal Access Token(s) used by the BFS crawler AND by the gimie
# hybrid path when enabled.
#
# Single-token deployments:
#   CRAWLER_GITHUB_TOKEN=ghp_aaa…
#
# Multi-token rotation (preferred for higher effective rate limit):
#   CRAWLER_GITHUB_TOKEN_POOL=ghp_aaa…,ghp_bbb…,ghp_ccc…
#
# If both are set, CRAWLER_GITHUB_TOKEN_POOL wins. The legacy GITHUB_TOKEN
# variable is still read as a deprecated fallback and logs a warning.
#
# Required scopes:
#   read:org      — required by gimie's GraphQL query (org avatarUrl/name/etc).
#                   Without it the hybrid gimie path returns INSUFFICIENT_SCOPES.
#   read:user     — recommended; gimie reads contributor profiles.
#   public_repo   — required for crawling public repos (or `repo` for private).
#
# A classic PAT scoped read:org + read:user + public_repo is the simplest
# choice. Fine-grained PATs work too but need org-level approval.
CRAWLER_GITHUB_TOKEN=
# CRAWLER_GITHUB_TOKEN_POOL=

# ----- Multi-platform crawling (v3.0+) -------------------------------------
#
# `CRAWLER_PLATFORMS` is the comma-separated list of hosts the crawler is
# allowed to dispatch seeds to. Default (when unset): "github.com" only.
# Add any combination of the hosts below.
#
# Per-host tokens follow `CRAWLER_TOKEN__<HOST>` where the host is uppercased
# with dots and dashes replaced by underscores. For rotation pools, use the
# `_POOL_` variant with a comma-separated list. Hosts marked ANONYMOUS work
# without a token; the token only raises rate limits.
#
# Example: enable HuggingFace + Zenodo + EPFL Infoscience + DataCite +
# OpenAlex (all anonymous-friendly) plus GitHub for the source-code edges:
#   CRAWLER_PLATFORMS=github.com,huggingface.co,zenodo.org,infoscience.epfl.ch,datacite.org,openalex.org
#
# CRAWLER_PLATFORMS=github.com

# ----- Optional: GitHub multi-token (new host-keyed env vars) --------------
#
# Equivalent to the legacy CRAWLER_GITHUB_TOKEN above, but follows the
# host-keyed naming convention used by every other platform. The legacy
# variables still work as a deprecated fallback.
#
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__GITHUB_COM=
# CRAWLER_TOKEN_POOL__GITHUB_COM=

# ----- Optional: GitLab (multi-instance) -----------------------------------
#
# Each self-hosted GitLab instance reads its own token env var. Anonymous
# mode works for public projects / users / groups; tokens unlock private
# data + raise rate limits. Recommended scope: `read_api` (or `read_user` +
# `read_repository` if you want finer-grained access).
#
# Provision tokens at https://<instance>/-/user_settings/personal_access_tokens
#
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__GITLAB_COM=
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__GITLAB_EPFL_CH=
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__GITLAB_ETHZ_CH=
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__RENKULAB_IO=
# (any other gitlab.* instance follows the same pattern)

# ----- Optional: Zenodo + sandbox ------------------------------------------
#
# ANONYMOUS by default — public Zenodo records / communities / users are
# readable without auth. Token raises rate limits.
#
# Provision at https://zenodo.org/account/settings/applications/tokens/new/
#
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__ZENODO_ORG=
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__SANDBOX_ZENODO_ORG=

# ----- Optional: EPFL Infoscience ------------------------------------------
#
# ANONYMOUS by default — public items / persons / orgunits readable without
# auth. Aggressive 429 rate-limiting on the anonymous tier; a token helps.
# Contact EPFL IT to provision a DSpace API token if needed.
#
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__INFOSCIENCE_EPFL_CH=

# ----- Optional: DataCite Commons ------------------------------------------
#
# ANONYMOUS by default — public /dois, /clients, search endpoints all return
# 200 without auth. The user-facing platform key is `datacite.org`, but the
# token env var uses the API host (`api.datacite.org`):
#
# Provision at https://commons.datacite.org/sign-in (DataCite members only)
#
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__API_DATACITE_ORG=
# CRAWLER_TOKEN_POOL__API_DATACITE_ORG=

# ----- Optional: Crossref polite-pool contact email (Spec 6) ---------------
#
# Crossref gives more consistent rate limits to requests that identify
# themselves. Optional but strongly recommended for production deployments.
# Set to your organisation's contact email address.
#
# CRAWLER_CROSSREF_MAILTO=you@example.org

# ----- Optional: OpenAlex polite-pool contact email -------------------------
#
# OpenAlex polite-pool contact email — identifying requests receive higher and
# more consistent rate limits from the OpenAlex API.
#
# CRAWLER_OPENALEX_MAILTO=you@example.org

# ----- Optional: HuggingFace -----------------------------------------------
#
# ANONYMOUS by default — public models / datasets / spaces / papers /
# collections all readable. Token raises rate limits + unlocks gated content.
#
# Provision at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens (read-only suffices)
#
# CRAWLER_TOKEN__HUGGINGFACE_CO=
# CRAWLER_TOKEN_POOL__HUGGINGFACE_CO=

# ----- Optional: data + cache directories ----------------------------------
#
# OPC_DATA_DIR: where the API stores per-job artifacts (graph snapshots,
# resumable state, JSON-LD payloads). Defaults to /tmp/open-pulse-crawler
# inside the container; change only if you mount a persistent volume.
# OPC_DATA_DIR=/tmp/open-pulse-crawler
#
# OPC_CACHE_DIR: where GitHub API responses are cached between crawls.
# Unset -> ${OPC_DATA_DIR}/cache for the API (writable in the container);
# the CLI uses data/open-pulse-crawler/cache. Empty -> caching disabled.
# An unwritable path disables caching with a warning rather than failing.
# OPC_CACHE_DIR=
#
# OPC_CACHE_TTL_DAYS: a cached API response older than this is treated as a
# miss and refetched, so the cache self-refreshes. Unset -> 30 days.
# Set to 0 to disable expiry (entries kept indefinitely).
# OPC_CACHE_TTL_DAYS=30

# ----- Optional: GUI password (only relevant with --profile gui) -----------
#
# Required by the Streamlit GUI to gate the browser interface. If unset, the
# GUI shows a visible warning and stays open. Pick anything non-trivial:
#   GUI_PASSWORD=$(python -c 'import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(16))')
# GUI_PASSWORD=

# ----- Optional: gimie hybrid (deployment-time, server-side) ---------------
#
# When enabled, the crawler enriches repository nodes from a gimie JSON-LD
# service (users/orgs still come from GitHub via PyGithub). These are server
# concerns, not per-request — clients of /api/v1/crawl don't see or pass them.
#
# Truthy values: true, 1, yes, on (case-insensitive). Anything else: false.
# GIMIE_ENABLED=false
# GIMIE_API_BASE=http://host.docker.internal:1234
# GIMIE_STORE_JSONLD=false
# GIMIE_SKIP_EXISTING_JSONLD=false

# ----- Optional: compose-only knobs ----------------------------------------
#
# These are read by infra/docker-compose.yml, not by the Python code.
#
# Override the published image tag (defaults to :latest on GHCR).
# OPC_IMAGE=ghcr.io/sdsc-ordes/open-pulse-crawler:1.0.0
#
# Host port for the FastAPI service (default profile, defaults to 8000).
# OPC_API_PORT=8000
#
# Host port for the Nginx reverse proxy (only with --profile gui, defaults to 80).
# OPC_PORT=8080
